#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:9
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"Teach agents how to capture valuable conversations and thinking as notes "
"in the Hero knowledge base. Notes are the lowest-friction knowledge type "
"— no structure required, no status workflow, just timestamped captures of"
" thinking that gets indexed and searchable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:13
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:15
msgid "Load this skill when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:16
msgid "A user asks you to \"save this conversation as a note\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:17
msgid ""
"A user says \"capture this\" or \"remember this\" or \"turn this into a "
"note\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:18
msgid ""
"You've had a particularly productive brainstorm or design discussion and "
"the user wants to preserve it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:19
msgid "A debugging session produced valuable insights worth recording"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:20
msgid "The user is dictating stream-of-consciousness thinking they want preserved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:22
msgid "The golden rule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:24
msgid ""
"**Include both sides of the conversation.** The agent's analysis, "
"reasoning, suggestions, and code examples are often the most valuable "
"part. Do not strip out your own contributions. Do not aggressively "
"summarize. Preserve the thinking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:26
msgid "How to capture a note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:28
msgid "Step 1: Determine the slug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:30
msgid "Derive a short kebab-case slug from the topic:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:31
msgid "`auth-flow-brainstorm`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:32
msgid "`redis-vs-postgres-session-store`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:33
msgid "`why-we-chose-grpc`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:34
msgid "`debugging-memory-leak-april-12`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:36
msgid ""
"If the user doesn't provide a topic, ask: \"What should I title this "
"note?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:38
msgid "Step 2: Create the note file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:40
msgid "Run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:41
msgid "hero note <slug>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:45
msgid ""
"This creates `.hero/knowledge/notes/<slug>/spec.md` with minimal "
"frontmatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:47
msgid "Step 3: Write the full content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:49
msgid ""
"Open the created file and replace the placeholder with the captured "
"content. Use this structure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:51
msgid ""
"---\n"
"title: <descriptive title>\n"
"type: note\n"
"created: <date>\n"
"tags: [<relevant>, <tags>]\n"
"---\n"
"# <Title>\n"
"\n"
"## Context\n"
"What prompted this conversation. One or two sentences.\n"
"\n"
"## Discussion\n"
"\n"
"**Human:** <user's message>\n"
"\n"
"**Assistant:** <your response>\n"
"\n"
"**Human:** <user's follow-up>\n"
"\n"
"**Assistant:** <your analysis>\n"
"\n"
"(Continue for the full relevant conversation)\n"
"\n"
"## Key Takeaways\n"
"- Bullet point the conclusions, decisions made, or open questions\n"
"- Include any action items that emerged\n"
"- Note anything that should become a spec later\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:81
msgid "Step 4: Confirm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:83
msgid "Tell the user:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:84
msgid "Where the note was saved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:85
msgid "How many key points were captured"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:86
msgid "Suggest tagging if they didn't specify tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:88
msgid "What to include vs. exclude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:90
msgid "Include"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:91
msgid "The full back-and-forth dialogue (both sides)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:92
msgid "Code snippets and examples discussed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:93
msgid "Architectural diagrams or data models sketched out"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:94
msgid "Trade-off analysis and reasoning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:95
msgid "Conclusions and decisions reached"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:96
msgid "Open questions that remain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:98
msgid "Exclude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:99
msgid "Greetings, pleasantries, and small talk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:100
msgid ""
"Repeated corrections of typos or misunderstandings (just include the "
"corrected version)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:101
msgid ""
"Tool output that's purely mechanical (e.g., full test suite output — "
"summarize instead)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:102
msgid "Sensitive information (credentials, tokens, personal data) — redact these"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:104
msgid "Different capture modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:106
msgid "Full conversation capture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:107
msgid ""
"The user says \"save this whole conversation as a note.\" Capture "
"everything substantive from the session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:109
msgid "Selective capture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:110
msgid ""
"The user says \"save the part about auth as a note.\" Extract only the "
"relevant portion of the conversation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:112
msgid "Live note mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:113
msgid ""
"The user says \"let's brainstorm about X — capture this as a note when "
"we're done.\" Continue the conversation normally, then at the end, save "
"everything discussed about X."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:115
msgid "Quick thought"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:116
msgid ""
"The user says \"note: we should probably add rate limiting to the API.\" "
"Just run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:117
msgid "hero note \"we should probably add rate limiting to the API\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:120
msgid "This creates a one-liner note. Fast, minimal friction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:122
msgid "Relationship to other knowledge types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:124
msgid "Notes are the entry point for knowledge. Over time, notes may graduate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "From"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "To"
msgstr ""

