msgid "When"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "Note about a pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "Convention (`/convention`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "The pattern is worth standardizing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "Note about a decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "Decision (`/decide`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "The decision needs formal documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "Note about a feature idea"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "Spec (`/design`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "The idea is ready to become actionable work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "Note about a bug pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "Bug spec (`/diagnose`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md
msgid "The pattern needs investigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:133
msgid ""
"When saving a note, if you notice it's really a decision or convention in"
" disguise, mention that to the user: \"This looks like it could be a "
"decision record. Want me to create a `/decide` instead?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:135
msgid "Notes are searchable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/note-capture/SKILL.md:137
msgid ""
"Once saved, notes are indexed by `hero index` and searchable via `hero "
"search`. The full text is indexed with FTS5 porter stemming, so even "
"rough notes become findable later."
msgstr ""

